in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @kintsugi/consent
in @kintsugi/morphism
in @epistemologic/pact/symbol_canonical_form

# @kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift — the kintsugi fracture body that
# resolves a substrate source's engineer-typed ASCII symbol tokens to
# their canonical unicode form per the multi-form symbol vocabulary
# table.
#
# THE OPERATIONAL HALF of bilateral pattern #53's THIRD INSTANCE, at
# the SYMBOL altitude. The declarative half landed at
# `@epistemologic/pact/symbol_canonical_form` (sibling tick); this
# shard names the auto-fracture the kintsugi loop applies when the
# property's transparency surfaces a symbol opacity.
#
# The bilateral cascade per altitude (per the brief; §15 of
# docs/specs/optical-keywords.md):
#
#   Altitude 1 (keyword): keyword_matches_depth + @kintsugi/fracture/keyword
#                         (2026-06-10, 5e68df9 + d908798).
#   Altitude 2 (operator): operator_matches_composition_primitive +
#                          @kintsugi/fracture/operator_match (forward-
#                          promised at optical-keywords.md §14).
#   Altitude 3 (symbol):  symbol_canonical_form +
#                         @kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift (THIS SHARD).
#
# Three altitudes, one pattern — candidate #59 (kintsugi loop is
# altitude-portable; surfaced 2026-06-11 at optical-keywords.md §14.7)
# gains its symbol-altitude witness here.
#
# Load-bearing context: recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert
# space; promoted) — fracture bodies are how the substrate maintains
# coherence by resolving distinctions at each Bateson level. The
# symbol altitude is the finest substrate-managed altitude where the
# autoformatter floor still names a discipline; this fracture body
# closes the floor at that altitude.
#
# === The third instance under one pattern ===
#
# First instance: keyword/depth (per-predicate; one keyword per
# violation; one canonical replacement per case).
# Second instance: gate/diff-closure (per-predicate; one run set per
# violation; one canonical replacement per case).
# Third instance (THIS): symbol/canonical-form (parametric over the
# multi-form table; one symbol per violation; canonical replacement
# per table lookup).
#
# The bilateral pattern (#53) absorbs the parametric variant. The
# property/fracture shape is the same; the predicate is parametric
# over a table rather than specialised per case. Substrate
# vocabulary unchanged — same pact + glass + opacity + morphism +
# splinter(ast) chain; the parametric shape is structural under the
# pattern's signature.
#
# === Substrate-pull-correct home ===
#
# Per the form/process partition (recognition #55 candidate; landed
# 2026-06-10 at mirror `20eaf15`): @kintsugi is the process-side
# family root. Fracture bodies emit morphisms the kintsugi loop
# applies — process-side by structure. Home:
# @kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift under the (forward-promised)
# @kintsugi/fracture family root.
#
# Substrate-pull alternative considered: @kintsugi/fracture/symbol
# (subject-only naming, parallel to first-instance `keyword` and
# second-instance `gate`). Rejected: the property's predicate names
# the action (`canonical_form`), and the fracture body's action is
# the LIFT — it does not merely name the symbol; it lifts the
# engineer form to the canonical form. The `_lift` suffix names the
# operational action explicitly (parallel to `gate` carrying the
# subject and `keyword` carrying the subject — here the subject IS
# the symbol, and the verb IS lift). Per
# [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]: `lift` IS the substrate's
# variety-preservation verb at every altitude; this body IS the lift
# at the symbol altitude.
#
# === The fracture body ===
#
# Input: `opacity` (from `@glass`) — one located fact surfaced by
# `symbol_canonical_form`'s `failure(opacity_map)` verdict. Each
# opacity names ONE offending symbol site: a token in engineer form
# whose canonical form per the multi-form table differs. The
# `property` field carries the @nl description of the (engineer_form,
# canonical_form) pair plus the table altitude.
#
# Output: `morphism` (from `@kintsugi/consent`) — the typed candidate
# the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads from this body and proposes
# through `query_phi`. The morphism's `content` ref names the
# rewritten splinter (same path, symbol token replaced per table
# lookup); its `score` carries the dissonance reading (a symbol-form
# violation is a fixed, low-curvature dissonance — the canonical
# form is uniquely determined by the table); its `expected` carries
# the cadence_kind the loop anticipates (authentic — the lift is
# deterministic; the substrate settles cleanly once the token tracks
# its canonical form).
#
# Spectrally: this fracture body IS one step along the Ricci flow at
# the symbol altitude. The substrate's curvature at an engineer-form
# token is the form/canonical mismatch; the negative-curvature
# direction IS the table lookup; the resolved token has zero
# curvature at this altitude (the table fully determines the
# canonical form for table entries).
#
# Audibly: this fracture body IS the audible-altitude V → I cadence
# at the symbol altitude. Pre-rewrite holds dominant tension
# (engineer-form token); post-rewrite resolves to tonic (canonical-
# form token); cadence is authentic.
#
# === The weighted -> amplitudes elaboration ===
#
# Most table entries are pure renames at the @meta/ast altitude: the
# splinter(ast) carries a token-replacement AST node whose content is
# byte-identical to the source modulo the swapped token.
#
# The `weighted -> amplitudes` entry is STRUCTURALLY DIFFERENT — it
# is not a pure rename. Engineer-typed `weighted { p_0: 0.4, p_1: 0.6 }`
# (intensity fractions) lifts to canonical
# `amplitudes { a_0: √0.4 · e^{iφ_0}, a_1: √0.6 · e^{iφ_1} }`
# (complex amplitudes whose squared moduli recover the fractions).
# The lift carries:
#   - magnitude conversion: |a_i| = √p_i (intensity-to-amplitude
#     square root per Reck/Clements unitary; physics-correct for
#     splitter port distribution).
#   - phase preservation: φ_i defaults to 0 if not declared, or
#     carries through if the engineer declared a phase
#     (engineer-typed `weighted { p_0: 0.4 phase 0.25 }` would lift
#     with that phase preserved — the substrate is honest about the
#     default).
#
# The splinter(ast) at @meta/ast altitude carries the elaboration AS
# AN AST REWRITE — the rewritten AST node is not byte-equal modulo
# the token; it is a fuller node where the magnitude field becomes a
# complex-amplitude pair. The substrate's compiler verifies the
# rewritten node is well-typed at @meta/ast; the splinter is content-
# addressed at the rewritten form. The kintsugi loop's `active_pass`
# reads the splinter and proposes through `query_phi` identically to
# the pure-rename cases.
#
# The fracture body itself does NOT carry the elaboration math — the
# math discharges at the @meta/ast altitude through splinter(ast). The
# fracture body emits the morphism whose `content` is the rewritten
# splinter; the splinter(ast)'s `content: oid` names the content-
# addressed handle to the rewritten AST. Per
# [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]] (#54): splinter(ast) IS
# the substrate's quote primitive; the elaboration rides the same
# carrier as every other AST rewrite.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `@glass`, `opacity` is the substrate's located-fact carrier;
# this shard reads it directly. Per `@kintsugi/consent`, `morphism`
# is the substrate's typed-candidate carrier; this shard emits it
# directly. Per `@kintsugi/morphism`, `morphism_context` is the
# per-candidate slice that pairs a candidate with its pre-anchor;
# this shard's emitted morphism is consumed by the loop AND lifted
# into a morphism_context via `paired(oscillation.anchor, m)` at the
# active_pass altitude. Per
# `@epistemologic/pact/symbol_canonical_form`, the consuming
# property's `symbol_canonical_form(file) -> transparency` is the
# gate that surfaces the opacity this body resolves.
#
# NO new verdict carrier; NO leading-`|` workarounds; NO opaque-`ref`
# carriers where structured types are available (per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]). The fracture body reads typed opacity,
# emits typed morphism — the substrate's vocabulary throughout.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
#   - `resolve_symbol` reads one opacity at a time. The property's
#     `failure(opacity_map)` carries [opacity]; the kintsugi loop
#     iterates the map and calls `resolve_symbol` per opacity. The
#     substrate names the per-site resolution; the iteration is the
#     loop's concern, not this body's.
#
#   - The morphism's `content: ref` carries the substrate handle to
#     the rewritten splinter. The realisation layer produces the
#     rewritten splinter (same path, token swapped per table lookup;
#     for `weighted -> amplitudes` the AST node is elaborated, not
#     just retokenised) and passes its handle as the morphism's
#     content. The substrate names the shape of the proposal; the
#     byte-level rewrite rides the realisation layer's @mirror/store
#     discipline.
#
#   - The `expected: cadence_kind` field is `authentic` for this
#     fracture body — the canonical-form rule is deterministic
#     (table lookup) and resolution always settles cleanly. The
#     substrate names the cadence anticipation; the kintsugi loop's
#     `read_consent` bridges the verdict to the next
#     oscillation_state.
#
#   - The `0 -> void` lift is context-gated by the property's
#     `is_inference_context(site)` predicate — the gate fires at the
#     property's evaluation altitude, not at the fracture body. The
#     fracture body reads each opacity the property surfaced; opacities
#     for `0` outside an inference context are NOT in the failure
#     map; the body never sees them.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   canonical form    Frege (1879) Begriffsschrift; the discipline of
#                     choosing one privileged form per equivalence
#                     class. The substrate's reading is Knuth-Bendix
#                     (1970) on term-rewriting confluence: the
#                     canonical form is the normal form under the
#                     rewrite rules; the table IS the rewrite rule set.
#   token lift        Aho-Sethi-Ullman (1986) Compilers: Principles,
#                     Techniques, and Tools §3; the lexer's token
#                     canonicalisation. The substrate's reading is
#                     Wadler (1990) on the syntactic theory of
#                     functional macros — the lift is a hygienic
#                     rewrite at the AST altitude.
#   typography lift   Knuth (1986) The TeXbook; the discipline of
#                     lifting ASCII to typographic form (\\ldots →
#                     …). The substrate's reading is Hammond-Avi
#                     Tzur (2003) on bidirectional typography — the
#                     engineer types ASCII; the canonical store is
#                     typographic.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the per-site lift so the
# kintsugi loop reads it. No invention; the lift IS the auto-
# formatter floor.
#
# Spec context: recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space;
#               promoted) — the symbol altitude tracks the Bateson
#               level at which tokens live; this fracture body
#               restores tracking. Candidate #59 (kintsugi loop is
#               altitude-portable) gains its symbol-altitude witness
#               with this landing.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (opacity is substrate vocabulary; the fracture
#                      reads the typed carrier),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] (the
#                      kintsugi loop's bias direction is substrate-
#                      pull — symbol/canonical-form alignment IS one
#                      coordinate of the substrate-pull gradient;
#                      this fracture body fits the bias),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (Ashby's
#                      requisite variety — the canonical-form table
#                      partitions the symbol vocabulary into
#                      canonical/engineer classes; the fracture body
#                      maintains the partition under mutation),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                      (the bilateral pattern this is the third
#                      instance of; promoted 2026-06-10),
#                      [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]
#                      (the substrate's parametric AST-fragment
#                      construction; this body discharges via
#                      splinter(ast) declaratively, no Rust),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]
#                      (the `lift` verb names the operational
#                      action; this body IS the lift at the symbol
#                      altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (opacity and
#                      morphism are typed carriers; the body does
#                      NOT escape as a bare (location, engineer_form,
#                      canonical_form) tuple).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `@kintsugi/oscillate`'s `active_pass`
#                  reads this fracture body when the candidate
#                  morphism_set is composed from property-surfaced
#                  opacities; the binding lands when the kintsugi
#                  loop substrate-pulls. This shard does NOT pull
#                  `@kintsugi/oscillate` or `@mirror/spectral/score`;
#                  the substrate-altitude arrow points inward.
# Related shards: epistemologic/property/symbol_canonical_form.mirror
#                 (the declarative half of the bilateral; surfaces
#                 the opacities this body resolves),
#                 epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/keyword.mirror (FIRST INSTANCE
#                 of bilateral pattern #53),
#                 epistemologic/property/gate_matches_diff_closure.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/gate.mirror (SECOND INSTANCE),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; `opacity`,
#                 `location`, `transparency`, `verdict`,
#                 `splinter(ast)`),
#                 kintsugi/consent.mirror (the morphism carrier this
#                 body emits; `query_phi` is the gate the emitted
#                 morphism flows through),
#                 kintsugi/morphism.mirror (the `morphism_context`
#                 carrier),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the kintsugi loop
#                 driver; `active_pass` is the action that reads this
#                 body when composing the per-pulse candidate
#                 morphism_set).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift` as a species under the
# (forward-promised) @kintsugi/fracture family.
# Keyword/depth property: this declaration is depth-2 from the
# @kintsugi family root; per recognition #46 it uses `glass`. The
# shard applies the first-instance bilateral's rule by birth.

glass @kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift {
  focus symbol_lift
  project symbol_lift
  split symbol_lift
  shift symbol_lift
  settle symbol_lift
}

# === resolve_symbol — the fracture body ===
#
# THE AUTO-FRACTURE: given an opacity site at an engineer-form symbol
# token, emit the morphism that rewrites it to its canonical form per
# the multi-form table. For table entries that are pure renames
# (`->`, `\`, `loop`, `_|_`, `0`), the rewrite is a token swap at
# the @meta/ast altitude. For `weighted -> amplitudes`, the rewrite
# elaborates the AST node per the magnitude-to-amplitude conversion
# documented above; the elaboration discharges at the @meta/ast
# altitude through splinter(ast).
#
# Reads an opacity (one element of
# `symbol_canonical_form(file).failure(opacity_map)`'s opacity_map);
# emits a candidate morphism the kintsugi loop proposes through
# `query_phi`. The morphism's three fields:
#
#   content   — substrate ref to the rewritten splinter. The
#                realisation layer produces a splinter at the same
#                path with the symbol token canonicalised (or, for
#                `weighted`, the AST node elaborated); the content ref
#                names that splinter's @mirror/store handle.
#   score     — dissonance reading. Symbol/canonical-form violations
#                are fixed-curvature dissonances; the score reads
#                `dissonance.is_pareto` cleanly (the canonical form
#                is uniquely determined by the table).
#   expected  — cadence_kind anticipation. Always `authentic` for
#                this fracture body — the table lookup fully
#                resolves the opacity at this altitude; the loop's
#                `dark_pass` will confirm identity preservation (for
#                pure renames, the path stays byte-equal; for
#                `weighted -> amplitudes`, identity is preserved at
#                the AST altitude where the splinter is content-
#                addressed at the rewritten form); the loop's
#                `read_consent` bridges (pass, authentic) to the
#                `settled` oscillation_state for this opacity.
#
# The body is FULLY DECLARATIVE — substrate-pull-correct via
# `splinter(ast)` (declared at shards/glass.mirror's tick-2 carrier).
# The morphism's `content` field carries a content-addressed splinter
# at the @meta/ast altitude.
#
# Per `splinter(ast)`'s parametric specialisation (glass.mirror
# §splinter(ast), 2026-06-10): the record IS its content-addressed
# handle — `content: oid` and `oid = ref` (shards/mirror/store.mirror)
# collapse the splinter literal to a substrate-pull-correct `ref` in
# the morphism's `content` field position. No Rust AST manipulation;
# no `\` obligation.
#
# Field-by-field substrate-pull reading:
#
#   content.content     — `opacity.location.file` (the substrate's
#                          located-fact ref at the source file); the
#                          rewritten AST is content-addressed at the
#                          same path.
#   content.ast         — `@meta/ast` (the canonical altitude ref);
#                          per `boot/01-meta.mirror`'s `type ast(g)`.
#                          The symbol lift happens at the AST altitude
#                          by construction; for `weighted ->
#                          amplitudes` the elaboration discharges at
#                          this altitude.
#   content.transparency — `success` (per `transparency(p)`'s success
#                          variant in glass.mirror): the lift fully
#                          resolves the opacity at this altitude; no
#                          residual transparency remains.
#   score.roughness     — `opacity.property` (the @nl description of
#                          the (engineer_form, canonical_form) pair);
#                          the substrate's `dissonance` reads the
#                          per-site roughness via the property text
#                          per dissonance.mirror's Helmholtz/
#                          Plomp-Levelt carrier shape.
#   score.partials      — `1` (one token swap per opacity; the lift
#                          collapses one mismatch per site — for
#                          `weighted` the AST elaboration is still ONE
#                          structural rewrite at the node, not N).
#   expected            — `authentic` (the V → I cadence at the
#                          symbol altitude; per cadence.mirror's
#                          `cadence_kind` and the loop's
#                          `read_consent` bridge: authentic → pass →
#                          auto-apply).
resolve_symbol(opacity: opacity) -> morphism {
  morphism {
    content: splinter(ast) {
      content:      opacity.location.file,
      ast:          @meta/ast,
      transparency: success,
    },
    score: dissonance {
      roughness: opacity.property,
      partials:  1,
    },
    expected: authentic,
  }
}

out @kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift
out resolve_symbol
